7. Priority-Aware Entanglement Scheduling

7.1 Weighted Max-Weight Stability

Theorem 7.1 (Weighted max-weight stability).
Consider $K$ traffic classes with arrival rates $\lambda_i$ and weights $w_i > 0$. If $\lambda \in \operatorname{int}(\Lambda)$, where $\Lambda$ is the capacity region, then the weighted max-weight policy (maximising $\sum_i w_i Q_i(t)\mu_i(t)$) yields

\limsup_{T\to\infty} \frac{1}{T} \sum_{t=0}^{T-1} \sum_{i=1}^{K} \mathbb{E}[Q_i(t)] < \infty.

Proof.
Define $L(Q) = \frac{1}{2}\sum_i w_i Q_i^2$. The Lyapunov drift is bounded by

\Delta(Q) \leq B - \sum_i w_i Q_i(\mathbb{E}[\mu_i|Q] - \lambda_i),

where $B$ is a constant depending on maximum arrival and service rates. Since $\lambda \in \operatorname{int}(\Lambda)$, there exists $\varepsilon > 0$ and a policy with $\mathbb{E}[\mu_i^*] \geq \lambda_i + \varepsilon$. By max-weight optimality, the chosen policy yields $\sum_i w_i Q_i \mathbb{E}[\mu_i^{\mathrm{MW}}|Q] \geq \sum_i w_i Q_i(\lambda_i + \varepsilon)$. Hence $\Delta(Q) \leq B - \varepsilon \sum_i w_i Q_i$. Summing over $t$ and taking the limit gives the result. $\square$

7.2 Strict-Priority Emergency Bound

Theorem 7.2 (Strict-priority queue bound).
Suppose class 1 has strict preemptive priority, with maximum service rate $\mu_1^{\max}$ and arrival rate $\lambda_1 < \mu_1^{\max}$. Let $\delta = \mu_1^{\max} - \lambda_1$. Then

\limsup_{T\to\infty} \frac{1}{T} \sum_{t=0}^{T-1} \mathbb{E}[Q_1(t)] \leq \frac{(A_{\max} + \mu_1^{\max})^2}{2\delta}.

Proof.
Use $V(Q_1) = \frac{1}{2}Q_1^2$. The drift is

\Delta V(Q_1) \leq Q_1(\lambda_1 - \mathbb{E}[\mu_1|Q_1]) + \frac{1}{2}(A_{\max} + \mu_1^{\max})^2.

For $Q_1 > 0$, strict priority gives $\mathbb{E}[\mu_1|Q_1] = \mu_1^{\max}$, so

\Delta V(Q_1) \leq B_1 - \delta Q_1,

with $B_1 = \frac{1}{2}(A_{\max} + \mu_1^{\max})^2$. Summing over time and taking the limit superior yields the bound. $\square$

